IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg5, layer 1.
-- Sections 221 (voting, inspection and other rights of bondholders and debenture holders) and 224 (form of records).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550).
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Section 221 deems the holders of obligations to be "stockholders" for the votes of stockholders that the chapter requires, if the certificate so provides;
-- the keel lists that deeming rule as encoded here (it is a predicate over one holder, not a change to the definition of stockholder elsewhere).
-- Its last clause refers to section 242(b)(2), which is in this piece (module dg5-s241-s242-amendment.l4): the outcome of that rule for the holder is taken here as a fact.
-- Sections 156, 159, 217(a), 218, 219 and 220 (piece dg3 and dg4) and Article 8 of Title 6 (not among the inputs) are named in section 224 as things the stock ledger must serve.

§ `Section 221 -- rights of the holders of bonds, debentures and other obligations`

-- src:891 | Every corporation may in its certificate of incorporation confer upon the holders of any bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation the power to vote in respect to the corporate affairs and management of the corporation to the extent and in the manner provided in the certificate of incorporation and may confer upon such holders of bonds, debentures or other obligations the same right of inspection of its books, accounts and other records, and also any other rights, which the stockholders of the corporation have or may have by reason of this chapter or of its certificate of incorporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 221 (src:891)
DECLARE `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation` HAS
    `the person holds bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to vote in respect to the corporate affairs and management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of incorporation confers the same right of inspection of the books, accounts and other records that the stockholders have` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of incorporation confers another right that the stockholders have` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of incorporation provides that the holders of obligations are deemed to be stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "the power to vote in respect to the corporate affairs and management of the corporation to the extent and in the manner provided in the certificate of incorporation".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 221 (src:891)
GIVEN h IS A `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 221 the holder of obligations may vote on the corporate affairs and management` h MEANS
        h's `the person holds bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation`
    AND h's `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to vote in respect to the corporate affairs and management`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 221 (src:891)
GIVEN h IS A `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 221 the holder of obligations has the stockholders' right of inspection` h MEANS
        h's `the person holds bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation`
    AND h's `the certificate of incorporation confers the same right of inspection of the books, accounts and other records that the stockholders have`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 221 (src:891)
GIVEN h IS A `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 221 the holder of obligations has another right that the stockholders have` h MEANS
        h's `the person holds bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation`
    AND h's `the certificate of incorporation confers another right that the stockholders have`

-- "If the certificate of incorporation so provides, such holders ... shall be deemed to be stockholders, and their bonds, debentures or other obligations shall be deemed to be shares of stock,
-- for the purpose of any provision of this chapter which requires the vote of stockholders as a prerequisite to any corporate action."
-- src:891 | If the certificate of incorporation so provides, such holders of bonds, debentures or other obligations shall be deemed to be stockholders, and their bonds, debentures or other obligations shall be deemed to be shares of stock, for the purpose of any provision of this chapter which requires the vote of stockholders as a prerequisite to any corporate action …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 221 (src:891)
GIVEN h IS A `dg5 s 221 Holder of obligations of the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 221 the holder of obligations is deemed a stockholder, and the obligation a share of stock, for a vote of stockholders required by the chapter` h MEANS
        h's `the person holds bonds, debentures or other obligations issued or to be issued by the corporation`
    AND h's `the certificate of incorporation provides that the holders of obligations are deemed to be stockholders`

-- "the certificate of incorporation may divest the holders of capital stock, in whole or in part, of their right to vote on any corporate matter whatsoever, except as set forth in § 242(b)(2)":
-- the class vote of section 242(b)(2) survives any divestiture (in range: module dg5-s241-s242-amendment.l4, `s 242(b)(2) the holder is entitled to vote as a class`).
-- src:891 | and the certificate of incorporation may divest the holders of capital stock, in whole or in part, of their right to vote on any corporate matter whatsoever, except as set forth in § 242(b)(2) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 221 (src:891)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation divests the holders of capital stock of their right to vote on the matter, in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is entitled to vote as a class on the matter under s 242(b)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 221 the holder of capital stock has been divested of the right to vote on the matter` `the certificate of incorporation divests the holders of capital stock of their right to vote on the matter, in whole or in part` `the holder is entitled to vote as a class on the matter under s 242(b)(2)` MEANS
        `the certificate of incorporation divests the holders of capital stock of their right to vote on the matter, in whole or in part`
    AND (NOT `the holder is entitled to vote as a class on the matter under s 242(b)(2)`)

§ `Section 224 -- form of records`

-- out of range: sections 219 and 220 (piece dg4)
-- out of range: sections 156 and 159 (piece dg3) and 217(a) and 218 (piece dg4)
-- out of range: Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6 (not among the inputs)
-- src:911 | Any records administered by or on behalf of the corporation in the regular course of its business, including its stock ledger, books of account, and minute books, may be kept on, or by means of, or be in the form of, any information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases (including 1 or more distributed electronic networks or databases), provided that the records so kept can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time, and, with respect to the stock ledger, that the records so kept (i) can be used to prepare the list of stockholders specified in §§ 219 and 220 of this title, (ii) record the information specified in §§ 156, 159, 217(a) and 218 of this title, and (iii) record transfers of stock as governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6. Any corporation shall convert any records so kept into clearly legible paper form upon the request of any person entitled to inspect such records pursuant to any provision of this chapter. When records are kept in such manner, a clearly legible paper form prepared from or by means of the information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases (including 1 or more distributed electronic networks or databases) shall be valid and admissible in evidence, and accepted for all other purposes, to the same extent as an original paper record of the same information would have been, provided the paper form accurately portrays the record.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 224 (src:911)
DECLARE `dg5 s 224 Records kept by the corporation` HAS
    `the records are kept on, or by means of, or in the form of, an information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the records can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the records are the stock ledger`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stock ledger can be used to prepare the list of stockholders specified in ss 219 and 220` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stock ledger records the information specified in ss 156, 159, 217(a) and 218`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stock ledger records transfers of stock as governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Any records "may be kept on, or by means of, or be in the form of, any information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases ..., provided that the records
-- so kept can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time, and, with respect to the stock ledger, that the records so kept (i) can be used to prepare the list of
-- stockholders ..., (ii) record the information specified in ..., and (iii) record transfers of stock ...". Sections 156, 159, 217(a), 218, 219, 220 are out of range (pieces dg3, dg4).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 224 (src:911)
GIVEN r IS A `dg5 s 224 Records kept by the corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 224 the records may be kept in that form` r MEANS
        r's `the records are kept on, or by means of, or in the form of, an information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases`
    AND r's `the records can be converted into clearly legible paper form within a reasonable time`
    AND (   (NOT r's `the records are the stock ledger`)
         OR (    r's `the stock ledger can be used to prepare the list of stockholders specified in ss 219 and 220`
             AND r's `the stock ledger records the information specified in ss 156, 159, 217(a) and 218`
             AND r's `the stock ledger records transfers of stock as governed by Article 8 of subtitle I of Title 6`))

-- out of range: sections 219 and 220 (piece dg4) and the other inspection sections of the chapter
-- src:911 | Any corporation shall convert any records so kept into clearly legible paper form upon the request of any person entitled to inspect such records pursuant to any provision of this chapter. When records are kept in such manner, a clearly legible paper form prepared from or by means of the information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases (including 1 or more distributed electronic networks or databases) shall be valid and admissible in evidence, and accepted for all other purposes, to the same extent as an original paper record of the same information would have been, provided the paper form accurately portrays the record.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 224 (src:911)
GIVEN `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asking is entitled to inspect the records pursuant to a provision of the chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 224 the corporation must convert the records into clearly legible paper form on the person's request` `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` `the person asking is entitled to inspect the records pursuant to a provision of the chapter` MEANS
        `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows`
    AND `the person asking is entitled to inspect the records pursuant to a provision of the chapter`

-- src:911 | When records are kept in such manner, a clearly legible paper form prepared from or by means of the information storage device, method, or 1 or more electronic networks or databases (including 1 or more distributed electronic networks or databases) shall be valid and admissible in evidence, and accepted for all other purposes, to the same extent as an original paper record of the same information would have been, provided the paper form accurately portrays the record.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 224 (src:911)
GIVEN `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paper form accurately portrays the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 224 the paper form is valid and admissible in evidence and accepted for all other purposes to the same extent as an original paper record` `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows` `the paper form accurately portrays the record` MEANS
        `the records are kept in a form that section 224 allows`
    AND `the paper form accurately portrays the record`
